# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: reports at least one platform")
val detected = is_linux() or is_macos() or is_windows()
expect(detected).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

### Play xvfb wrap_cmd

#### returns the same command on macOS

- Verify: returns the same command on macOS
   - Expected: cmd equals `npm`
   - Expected: args[0] equals `test`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: returns the same command on macOS")
if is_macos():
    val (cmd, args) = wrap_cmd("npm", ["test"])
    expect(cmd).to_equal("npm")
    expect(args[0]).to_equal("test")
```

</details>

#### returns the same command on Windows

- Verify: returns the same command on Windows
   - Expected: cmd equals `npm`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: returns the same command on Windows")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
if is_windows():
    val (cmd, args) = wrap_cmd("npm", ["test"])
    expect(cmd).to_equal("npm")
```

</details>

### Play xvfb maybe_wrap_cmd

#### does not wrap when force is false on macOS

- Verify: does not wrap when force is false on macOS
   - Expected: cmd equals `echo`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: does not wrap when force is false on macOS")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
if is_macos():
    val (cmd, args) = maybe_wrap_cmd("echo", ["hi"], false)
    expect(cmd).to_equal("echo")
```

</details>

